# More declarations reach a free name than any table of the translator once
# held. r reads box\v, and nothing in its sight declares box. Seventy
# declarations D00 to D69 have v, every second one after a field r does not
# use; v is 100 and the declaration's number. Seventy callers each hold a
# reference to the Structure of one declaration under the name box and
# call mid, which only hands the name on: the reader's input is formed at
# one call, with every one of the seventy as a possible declaration. Each
# caller gets its own v and one: 101 to 170. Entry 7.
D00:
    int: v 100
end: D00

